From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:03:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read video files and start their players off the UI thread

- startVideo asked VLC to read the file's tracks and waited for it, up to
  the parse limit, on the UI thread; now the parse runs on VLC's thread and
  each frame checks whether it ended. A file read once is not parsed again
  while its size and date stay the same.
- A VLC player opens its audio output when it is made (ALSA reads its
  configuration and probes every card, hundreds of ms on a handheld) and
  waits for its threads when stopped: one worker thread makes, starts,
  stops and releases them. The frames' buffers go with the player until it
  is released; until its first frame the snapshot or what is under the
  video shows.
